codex
The generic proof is still within normal resources, but it is slower than expected because the source’s short-circuit expressions split arbitrary incoming accumulator Booleans. I’m allowing this run a little longer; if it remains unresolved, the next refinement will encode the one-iteration Boolean update directly so the solver sees the fold identity syntactically.
