codex
The branch cap exposed the real explosion: unconstrained `Val` keys include dangling heap references, so the call machinery explores arbitrarily long dereference chains. Those are not well-formed keys in the theorem’s initial empty heap (and model mutable, unhashable Python objects), so I’m adding the semantic well-formedness condition “no reference-valued key.” Direct strings, numbers, booleans, tuples, `None`, and every other non-reference value remain symbolic and unbounded.
apply patch
