The joint run is not reusing the sibling claim as a lemma in the target proof; K’s claim selection proves obligations but does not automatically establish a reusable theorem database. I’ll use the standard two-command composition: first prove `loop` untrusted, then prove `target` with exactly that already-proved claim selected as a trusted auxiliary. The trust ledger will identify it as machine-proved evidence, not an external assumption.
