The direct frozen-method summary reached the right equality but triggered a backend `ErrorBottomTotalFunction` while normalizing the symbolic scope map—a concrete backend failure, not a false residual. I’m retaining the semantically exact constructor-level method twin, whose bridge-free theorem already covers every `str(CS)`, and restoring the guarded code destructor so the backend can represent that Boolean without crashing.
apply patch
